{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the sunlight strangely pixelated as it streamed through his window. He sat up, a disorientation washing over him unlike anything he'd ever experienced. His bedroom wasn't quite *right*. The colors were too vibrant, the textures too sharp. He reached out to touch his bedside table, and his hand passed right through it, leaving a faint shimmer in the air. A notification popped up in his vision: \"Welcome, Arthur! You have entered Aethelgard, a fantasy RPG. Level 1 achieved!\" Panic seized him. He looked down at his hands – they were no longer his own, but rendered in a blocky, almost cartoonish style. A health bar and mana pool floated above his head. This wasn't a dream. This was… a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, the floor feeling strangely solid despite its digital appearance. Outside, the world was breathtakingly unreal. Towering trees with impossibly green leaves swayed in a gentle breeze, and fantastical creatures – a griffin soaring overhead, a small, furry creature with oversized ears scampering through the grass – populated the landscape. A quest marker appeared on his HUD, pointing towards a nearby village. \"Retrieve lost artifact from Goblin Camp,\" it read. Arthur groaned. He was no hero, just a mid-level accountant with a penchant for spreadsheets. But there was no escape. He was trapped in Aethelgard, a pawn in someone else's game, and he had a feeling his life was about to get a whole lot more complicated.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.32705190777778625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002044230350293219}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.10078337788581848}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logprob": -1.43425714969635}, {"token": "▁strangely", "logprob": -1.9413211345672607}, {"token": "▁pixel", "logprob": -0.5138242244720459}, {"token": "at